what's done:

Database Schema: Comprehensive SQLite setup with proper migrations, foreign keys, and indexes
Authentication: JWT implementation with 2FA support and Google OAuth
Core Features: Chat, friends, matches, and notifications are functionally implemented
Architecture: Clean MVC pattern with proper separation of concerns
Error Handling: Well-structured custom error classes




Model / Service (business logic + database logic)
Controller (HTTP logic)
Connects HTTP requests to your model
Routes (URL mapping)
Purpose:
Bind URLs + HTTP methods to controllers


/////////////chat /////////////////

Prevents self-chat
Self-join: this says fetch any chat where user A is a participant and there is a message sent by user B (cp2.user_id) that is not blocked. 
Protection rules


❌ Chat must not already exist
❌ User2 must exist 
✔ Prevents self-chat ❌ Cannot chat with yourself
✔ Enforces chat membership
✔ Handles blocking cleanly
✔ Uses soft-blocking (blocks_active)
✔ Efficient SQL with joins
✔ Clean separation of concerns


Common errors:
400 Bad Request — missing user2_id or trying to create chat with yourself
404 Not Found — user with id 42 doesn't exist
401 Unauthorized — missing/invalid JWT



////////////friends////////////

✅ Receiver exists

❌ Sender ≠ Receiver

❌ Sender has blocked receiver → error

⚠️ Receiver blocked sender → request still created, but no notification

❌ Friendship already exists (accepted or pending)
Request exists

Only the receiver can respond

Cannot accept twice

Cannot act on cancelled requests

Cancel a pending request (sender only)

Unfriend an accepted friend (either user)
❌ Cannot modify declined requests

❌ Cannot unfriend twice

❌ Only sender can cancel pending request